---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Countries"
  description="nstate country chapters — fork the methodology to audit your government. Any country, any language."
>
  <div class="container">
    <div class="page-header">
      <div class="breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">nstate</a> / <span>countries</span>
      </div>
      <h1>Countries</h1>
      <p class="page-sub">
        The methodology is country-agnostic. Fork the template, adapt your data sources,
        and open a PR. Every country deserves a forensic audit of how it spends public money.
      </p>
    </div>

    <hr class="divider" />

    <!-- Active chapters -->
    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-label">active chapters</div>
      <div class="country-grid">
        <a href="/uk" class="country-card country-card--active">
          <div class="country-card__header">
            <span class="country-card__code">UK</span>
            <span class="badge badge--amber">active</span>
          </div>
          <h2 class="country-card__name">United Kingdom</h2>
          <p class="country-card__desc">
            The founding chapter. ONS, HMRC, OBR, DfE, DWP, Ofgem, Cabinet Office.
            First scorecards in progress.
          </p>
          <div class="country-card__stats">
            <div class="stat">
              <span class="stat__val">3</span>
              <span class="stat__label">in pipeline</span>
            </div>
            <div class="stat">
              <span class="stat__val">0</span>
              <span class="stat__label">published</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <hr class="divider" />

    <!-- How to start -->
    <section class="section" id="start">
      <div class="section-label">start a chapter</div>
      <h2>how it works</h2>
      <p class="section-sub">
        A country chapter is a folder in the nstate repository with its own data sources,
        pipelines, and scorecards. You bring the knowledge of your government;
        the methodology and template are already built.
      </p>

      <div class="steps">
        <div class="step">
          <div class="step__num">01</div>
          <h3>fork or open an issue</h3>
          <p>
            Open a GitHub issue titled "Country chapter: [your country]" with your name,
            country, and a primary data source you will use for the first scorecard.
            We will create a folder and add you as a chapter maintainer.
          </p>
          <a href="https://github.com/nstate-project/nstate/issues" class="link-arrow" target="_blank" rel="noopener">open an issue →</a>
        </div>

        <div class="step">
          <div class="step__num">02</div>
          <h3>copy the country template</h3>
          <p>
            Copy <code>COUNTRY-TEMPLATE.md</code> from the repo root into
            <code>your-country/README.md</code>. Fill in your national data sources
            and the equivalent of the Open Government Licence for your jurisdiction.
          </p>
          <a href="https://github.com/nstate-project/nstate/blob/main/COUNTRY-TEMPLATE.md" class="link-arrow" target="_blank" rel="noopener">view template →</a>
        </div>

        <div class="step">
          <div class="step__num">03</div>
          <h3>first scorecard PR</h3>
          <p>
            Follow the scorecard template in <code>METHODOLOGY.md</code>. Submit your
            first scorecard via PR. The nstate methodology team will review the evidence
            quality rating and data sourcing before merging.
          </p>
          <a href="/methodology" class="link-arrow">read the methodology →</a>
        </div>

        <div class="step">
          <div class="step__num">04</div>
          <h3>get listed here</h3>
          <p>
            Once your first scorecard is merged and the data pipeline is live,
            your chapter is listed on this page. You are the maintainer —
            nstate does not control country chapter editorial direction.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <hr class="divider" />

    <!-- Why it matters -->
    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-label">why international</div>
      <h2>governments compete on accountability when you measure them</h2>
      <p class="section-sub">
        Every government has audit bodies. Almost none publish their findings in
        a format that is comparable, reproducible, and citizen-facing.
        nstate exists to change that.
      </p>
      <div class="why-grid">
        <div class="why-item">
          <h3>comparable methodology</h3>
          <p>The same scorecard template works for any country. UK civil service productivity and German civil service productivity become directly comparable.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="why-item">
          <h3>no political capture</h3>
          <p>Chapter maintainers are independent. nstate provides the methodology. Countries provide the data and the analysis. Political affiliation of maintainers must be disclosed.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="why-item">
          <h3>fork if you disagree</h3>
          <p>If a national government successfully pressures a chapter, the community can fork it. The data and methodology are CC BY 4.0. Capture is not permanent.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="cta-block">
      <div>
        <strong>Ready to start?</strong>
        <p>The fastest path is to open a GitHub issue with your country and first data source.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cta-block__btns">
        <a href="https://github.com/nstate-project/nstate/issues" class="btn btn--primary" target="_blank" rel="noopener">open an issue ↗</a>
        <a href="/contribute" class="btn btn--ghost">contribution guide</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .page-header {
    padding: 3rem 0 2rem;
  }

  .breadcrumb {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--text-3);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .breadcrumb a {
    color: var(--amber);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .page-header h1 {
    font-size: 2.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .page-sub {
    color: var(--text-2);
    max-width: 60ch;
  }

  .section {
    padding: 3rem 0;
  }

  .section-label {
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--amber);
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .section h2 {
    font-size: 1.6rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .section-sub {
    color: var(--text-2);
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    max-width: 60ch;
  }

  /* Country grid */
  .country-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(280px, 1fr));
    gap: 1px;
    background: var(--border);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .country-card {
    background: var(--bg);
    padding: 1.75rem;
    text-decoration: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    transition: background 0.15s;
  }

  .country-card:hover {
    background: var(--surface);
  }

  .country-card__header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
  }

  .country-card__code {
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--text-3);
  }

  .country-card__name {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .country-card__desc {
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--text-2);
    max-width: none;
    flex: 1;
  }

  .country-card__stats {
    display: flex;
    gap: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 1rem;
    margin-top: auto;
  }

  .stat {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.15rem;
  }

  .stat__val {
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .stat__label {
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    color: var(--text-3);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }

  /* Steps */
  .steps {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(220px, 1fr));
    gap: 2rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .step {
    border-top: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 1.25rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.6rem;
  }

  .step__num {
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--amber);
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }

  .step h3 {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .step p {
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--text-2);
    flex: 1;
    max-width: none;
  }

  .link-arrow {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--amber);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .link-arrow:hover {
    opacity: 0.8;
  }

  /* Why grid */
  .why-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(240px, 1fr));
    gap: 2rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .why-item {
    border-top: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 1.25rem;
  }

  .why-item h3 {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .why-item p {
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--text-2);
    max-width: none;
  }

  /* CTA block */
  .cta-block {
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding: 2rem;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 4rem;
  }

  .cta-block strong {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
  }

  .cta-block p {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--text-2);
    max-width: none;
  }

  .cta-block__btns {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .btn {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: var(--font);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    padding: 0.7rem 1.4rem;
    text-decoration: none;
    border: 1px solid transparent;
    transition: background 0.15s, color 0.15s, border-color 0.15s;
  }

  .btn--primary {
    background: var(--amber);
    color: var(--bg);
    border-color: var(--amber);
  }

  .btn--primary:hover {
    background: #e6b800;
    color: var(--bg);
  }

  .btn--ghost {
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--text-2);
    border-color: var(--border-2);
  }

  .btn--ghost:hover {
    color: var(--text);
    border-color: var(--text-3);
  }
</style>
